Well, yes. AI tends to just create garbage and unless you know JS and logic well enough to tell its nonsense, you wont know know its feeding you garbage, much less know how to "fix" it. If by mentioning your inexperience that youre implying that youre also trying to learn, id suggest not relying on AI at all and do tutorials instead.
i dont know if you want both enemies and actors to have this shared TP system. you never mentioned enemies, but youre overwriting Game_Battler methods and are affecting both actors and enemies. You also only ever (try to) update the party's TPs and not the troop's. if an enemy were to run gainTp, youd still try to increase and update the party's TP. Then logically, making gainTp run gainTp on all actors can only cause an infinite loop.
...also the function that gives battlers tp for acting is gainSilentTp, so none of that would actually be ran in the first place outside of skill/item effect
